Bootstrap: docker
From: python@sha256:2325bb286ec344af3e5898cc224b5844e2707ac6e26b1632516fd3edc84a5e26

# =============================================================================
# bx_retip_train / DEF version 1.0
#
# [PURPOSE AND TARGET]
#   RTpred (Retip) module "train": runs `python -m mdcc.cli train`.
#   Revised from the received containers/train.def (Pipeline RTpred,
#   Revision 2) to follow the CLOSHA DEF policy; the image content (Python
#   packages, apt packages, mdcc code) is unchanged.
#   The mdcc package is embedded with %files, as in the
#   received DEF. Build from defs/Retip, because %files paths are relative to
#   the directory where `apptainer build` is run (checked with Apptainer 1.4.5).
#
# [INPUT AND OUTPUT STRUCTURE]
#   Defined by mdcc.cli train (see `--help`). Output directories must be
#   empty; the module refuses to write into a non-empty directory.
#
# [REQUIRED RUNTIME DEPENDENCIES]
#   Python 3.13.15 (official python image). mdcc.core.check_runtime requires
#   exactly numpy 2.3.5, pandas 2.3.3, rdkit 2026.3.1, autogluon.tabular
#   1.5.0, scikit-learn 1.7.1, scipy 1.16.3, lightgbm 4.6.0, catboost 1.2.10.
#   mdcc imports only numpy, pandas, rdkit, matplotlib, autogluon, sklearn,
#   and the standard library; it starts no subprocesses and uses no network.
#   apt: libgomp1 (LightGBM/CatBoost OpenMP), libstdc++6, fonts-dejavu-core.
#   Runtime analysis needs no network access.
#
# [BASE IMAGE AND INSTALLATION RULES FOR THIS DEF]
#   Base image: python:3.13.15-slim-bookworm (Debian 12.15), pinned by its
#   index digest in From. Debian 12 is not in the policy's base OS list
#   (Rocky Linux 9+, Ubuntu 22+); the user confirmed it runs on the target
#   systems, and the policy decision is pending.
#   Python packages: the requirements.txt pins were resolved for cp313
#   manylinux x86_64 into the 46-package lock below; every SHA256 matches the
#   PyPI JSON metadata, and pip installs with --require-hashes
#   --only-binary=:all:, so no source distribution is built.
#   %files content is verified before any installation: mdcc against the
#   SHA256 list in this DEF.
#   The uploaded mdcc must not contain Python bytecode caches (__pycache__):
#   they are not covered by the SHA256 list, so the build stops if any is
#   present instead of deleting them.
#   No Conda or Anaconda repository is used.
#
# [HPC BUILD REQUIREMENTS]
#   Use a designated build environment and an unprivileged build account.
#   Do not bind production data or shared system directories into the build container.
#   Host-side %pre and %setup sections are not used.
#   Build workspace: the fixed container-private path /__closha_build/work,
#   created with plain mkdir; the APT package cache (Dir::Cache), APT index
#   lists (Dir::State::lists), the pip lock file, pip temporary files
#   (TMPDIR), and HOME are placed below it, and only that path is removed
#   after separate checks. The received APT list deletion (/var/lib/apt/lists/*) is
#   replaced by this workspace cleanup. The base image may ship APT cleanup
#   hooks (docker-clean); they were not inspected.
#   The Apptainer output SIF, image cache, and build temporary files are host
#   artifacts; place them in an approved build workspace, separate from services.
#
# [RUNTIME ENVIRONMENT ISOLATION]
#   PATH is fixed without home entries; PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1 keeps host
#   ~/.local packages out. MPLCONFIGDIR follows the job's TMPDIR and is made
#   unique per user (the received fixed /tmp/mdcc-matplotlib path could
#   collide between users on a shared node).
#
# [CHANGES FROM THE RECEIVED DEF]
#   Added: host-isolation blocks (policy 6.1), the fixed build workspace and
#   APT cache redirection (policy 6), %files content verification, the
#   hash-locked pip install, `set -eu` in %test (the received %test passed
#   whatever the earlier checks returned), package import checks, this
#   header, and %help. containers/requirements.txt is no longer copied: the
#   lock is embedded here. Image packages and versions are unchanged.
#
# [VALIDATION STATUS AND REPRODUCIBILITY]
#   Checked: received DEF and requirements.txt, mdcc imports, models/
#   SHA256SUMS (235 files, all matching, none unlisted), the pip lock against
#   PyPI, the base image commands (mount, stat, awk, realpath, sha256sum),
#   and DEF %post and %test shell syntax (sh -n).
#   Isolation blocks updated on 2026-10-06 after a production build log:
#   the production build account has no /etc/subuid entry, so Apptainer runs
#   %post under the fakeroot command with read-only helpers under
#   /.singularity.d/libs and the host devtmpfs /dev and /dev/shm. The mount
#   allowlist now accepts those, and /dev/shm is covered with a private
#   tmpfs (same blocks as the ATAC-seq DEFs).
#   Local test builds (2026-10-07, GitHub Codespace, Apptainer 1.4.5 with
#   the production apptainer.conf, built from defs/Retip) succeeded as root
#   and with --fakeroot, including %test (check_runtime, package imports,
#   and `mdcc.cli train --help`).
#   Root builds were traced with strace: no process opened any /proc or /sys
#   path for writing, and host sysctl values did not change. inotify and
#   before/after listings showed no DEF-caused change in the host /tmp or
#   /var/tmp. Host events seen during the builds came from other sources:
#   the --fakeroot engine's empty /tmp/bind-mount-* directory (Apptainer,
#   before %post) and SQLite temporary files (/var/tmp/etilqs_*) written
#   every 10 s by a VS Code extension process, identified with strace.
#   Later on 2026-10-07 the mdcc/models checks were rewritten to satisfy the
#   site command blacklist (no directory changes and no deletion through
#   find), and mdcc must now be uploaded without __pycache__. This version
#   passed local root and --fakeroot rebuilds the same day with the same host
#   checks (no DEF-caused host /tmp, /var/tmp, /proc, /sys, or sysctl change).
#   A production build (fakeroot-command mode) of this version passed the
#   tmpfs mounts, the mount allowlist, the workspace setup, and the mdcc
#   SHA256 check, then stopped as designed because the uploaded mdcc held
#   __pycache__; the rest of %post has not yet run in production.
#   The new start blocks also passed in fakeroot-command mode (an account
#   without /etc/subuid entries) in a test DEF on ubuntu:24.04; a full build
#   in that mode was not run locally.
#   Not performed: a build on the production build machine, or analysis
#   runs with real input data.
#   Build from a shell without APPTAINER_* or SINGULARITY_* bind variables.
#   APT package versions may change between builds; they are recorded.
#
# [CHANGELOG]
#   2026-10-01 / 1.0: Policy-aligned revision of the received train.def.
# =============================================================================

%labels
    Pipeline RTpred
    Revision 2
    Module train
    Name bx_retip_train
    Version 1.0
    BaseOS Debian-12-bookworm
    Python 3.13.15
    PackageManager pip
    RuntimeNetworkRequired false

%files
    mdcc /opt/mdcc/mdcc

%environment
    export PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
    export PYTHONPATH=/opt/mdcc
    export PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1
    export PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
    export MPLBACKEND=Agg
    export MPLCONFIGDIR="${TMPDIR:-/tmp}/mdcc-matplotlib-$(id -u)"
    export OMP_NUM_THREADS=2
    export OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS=2
    export MKL_NUM_THREADS=2
    export HF_HUB_OFFLINE=1
    export AWS_EC2_METADATA_DISABLED=true

%post
    set -eu
    # Fixed container PATH; ignore any inherited PATH that may point into a
    # host-bound home directory.
    export PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
    export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8

    # Apptainer builds keep the admin "mount tmp = yes" setting, so %post sees
    # the host /tmp and /var/tmp. Cover both with private tmpfs mounts in this
    # container's mount namespace before any other command runs; the host
    # directories are then unreachable. If mounting fails, the build stops.
    mount -t tmpfs -o mode=1777,nosuid,nodev closha-tmp /tmp
    mount -t tmpfs -o mode=1777,nosuid,nodev closha-vartmp /var/tmp
    [ "$(stat -f -c %T /tmp)" = tmpfs ] || { echo "/tmp is not private" >&2; exit 1; }
    [ "$(stat -f -c %T /var/tmp)" = tmpfs ] || { echo "/var/tmp is not private" >&2; exit 1; }
    # With "mount dev = yes" the build may see the host's /dev and its shared
    # /dev/shm. Cover /dev/shm with a private tmpfs as well, then confirm from
    # the mount table that the newest /dev/shm mount is this one.
    if [ -d /dev/shm ]; then
        mount -t tmpfs -o mode=1777,nosuid,nodev closha-shm /dev/shm
        awk '$5 == "/dev/shm" { s = $0 } END { exit !(s ~ / - tmpfs closha-shm /) }' /proc/self/mountinfo ||
            { echo "/dev/shm is not private" >&2; exit 1; }
    fi
    # Record the mount table in the build log for review.
    cat /proc/self/mountinfo

    # Stop before any install step if the build container has a mount other
    # than those Apptainer creates for builds: the rootfs, /tmp and /var/tmp
    # (now covered above), private /etc/hosts and /etc/resolv.conf copies, and
    # kernel pseudo-filesystems under /dev, /proc, and /sys, plus, in builds
    # that run %post under the fakeroot command (no /etc/subuid entry), the
    # read-only fakeroot helpers Apptainer places under /.singularity.d/libs.
    # This rejects host paths added through APPTAINER_BINDPATH or
    # APPTAINER_MOUNT, which the build passes into %post from the caller's
    # environment.
    awk '
        { split($0, sep, " - "); split(sep[2], f, " "); mp = $5; opt = $6; fs = f[1]; src = $4 }
        mp == "/" || mp == "/tmp" || mp == "/var/tmp" { next }
        (mp == "/etc/hosts" || mp == "/etc/resolv.conf") &&
            src ~ /\/bundle-temp-[0-9]+\/(hosts|resolv\.conf)$/ { next }
        (mp == "/dev" || mp ~ /^\/dev\//) && fs ~ /^(devtmpfs|tmpfs|devpts|mqueue|hugetlbfs)$/ { next }
        (mp == "/proc" || mp ~ /^\/proc\//) && fs ~ /^(proc|binfmt_misc|autofs)$/ { next }
        (mp == "/sys" || mp ~ /^\/sys\//) &&
            fs ~ /^(sysfs|cgroup|cgroup2|securityfs|selinuxfs|debugfs|tracefs|bpf|fusectl|configfs|pstore|efivarfs)$/ { next }
        mp == "/.singularity.d/libs" && fs == "tmpfs" && opt ~ /^ro(,|$)/ { next }
        mp ~ /^\/\.singularity\.d\/libs\/(fakeroot|faked|libfakeroot\.so)$/ && opt ~ /^ro(,|$)/ { next }
        { print "Unexpected mount in build container: " mp " (" fs ")" > "/dev/stderr"; bad = 1 }
        END { exit bad }
    ' /proc/self/mountinfo || { echo "Build stopped: remove extra bind settings and rebuild" >&2; exit 1; }

    fail() { echo "Build check failed: $*" >&2; exit 1; }

    # Fixed container-private workspace from the approved profile.
    # Plain mkdir (no -p) fails if a path already exists, including a symlink
    # or a bind mount point, so the build stops instead of reusing it.
    BUILD_ROOT=/__closha_build
    WORK=/__closha_build/work
    mkdir -m 0700 -- "$BUILD_ROOT"
    mkdir -m 0700 -- "$WORK"
    mkdir -p -- "$WORK/tmp" "$WORK/home" "$WORK/py" \
        "$WORK/apt-cache/archives/partial" "$WORK/apt-lists/partial"

    # The admin config may bind the host home, and /tmp may be host-backed.
    # Redirect HOME, TMPDIR, and XDG directories into the workspace before any
    # other command runs, so no tool reads or writes host user files or /tmp.
    export HOME="$WORK/home"
    export TMPDIR="$WORK/tmp"
    export XDG_CACHE_HOME="$WORK/home/.cache"
    export XDG_CONFIG_HOME="$WORK/home/.config"
    export XDG_DATA_HOME="$WORK/home/.local/share"

    # The locked wheel hashes below are for x86_64 only.
    [ "$(dpkg --print-architecture)" = amd64 ] || fail "unsupported architecture"

    # Verify the mdcc code copied by %files before using it.
    [ ! -L /opt/mdcc/mdcc ] || fail "mdcc is a symlink"
    printf '%s\n' \
        '4a8e11aa2203596ffb4fa86b936834736d4b83c652c0a17a6c8c8a6219ccb6ae  /opt/mdcc/mdcc/__init__.py' \
        'a4b8cc22d61d4c8c06ad913adbbb160b7a449b3fc8bd08deb48064b8b2661db4  /opt/mdcc/mdcc/cli.py' \
        'ce4e1d86d65f2c973097ce7444f6b7097267846c8da5c5dea9546b763824424d  /opt/mdcc/mdcc/core.py' \
        'b32286871b0c833f3035adcceead1999f8219e13537c29fd4ecb885389f2c7d0  /opt/mdcc/mdcc/descriptors.py' \
        '53193f861da75ae844082728af4d82f161a7d7d53fcc22e0e6f3dcfeac42333d  /opt/mdcc/mdcc/preprocess.py' \
        '3697dffddf3bbdc2d71e2761f34ebebb98eba91b36aa10a4f48909ec1ad59e3d  /opt/mdcc/mdcc/pyretip/__init__.py' \
        'a7f9df1ed1e4e1195753730a1fae294ce924fba61e634500c60a4251e680855a  /opt/mdcc/mdcc/pyretip/trainer.py' \
        > "$WORK/mdcc.sha256"
    sha256sum --check --quiet "$WORK/mdcc.sha256"
    # Host-built bytecode caches are not covered by the SHA256 list and Python
    # could load them instead of the verified sources, so the upload must not
    # contain any; nothing is deleted here.
    [ -z "$(find /opt/mdcc/mdcc -name __pycache__ -print)" ] \
        || fail "mdcc contains __pycache__; upload mdcc without it"
    [ "$(find /opt/mdcc/mdcc -type f | wc -l)" = 7 ] \
        || fail "mdcc contains unexpected files"

    # Use the official base; APT cache and index lists stay in the workspace.
    export DEBIAN_FRONTEND=noninteractive
    apt-get -o Dir::Cache="$WORK/apt-cache" -o Dir::State::lists="$WORK/apt-lists" update
    apt-get -o Dir::Cache="$WORK/apt-cache" -o Dir::State::lists="$WORK/apt-lists" \
        install -y --no-install-recommends libgomp1 libstdc++6 fonts-dejavu-core

    # Hash-locked binary wheels (cp313, manylinux x86_64). Hashes match PyPI.
    export PIP_DISABLE_PIP_VERSION_CHECK=1
    export PIP_NO_CACHE_DIR=1
    printf '%s\n' \
        'autogluon.common==1.5.0 --hash=sha256:8d7f348acafe9c32c2ff49905dbcd652064ca8bb9359516dac05c32dd27409ad' \
        'autogluon.core==1.5.0 --hash=sha256:df60d751d4093decdbc5fbcc4498d3e6b3d66eba27761020a9f5d89c7b735a48' \
        'autogluon.features==1.5.0 --hash=sha256:5c8a7dd60c66b532b42122ff87a2d140adf7952632b6db24fe6255bb75f8d90e' \
        'autogluon.tabular==1.5.0 --hash=sha256:62ba6ee7fc88f60effc5e11ee6f55f86a0917b55f2c2ff881cd9a611267cdceb' \
        'boto3==1.43.106 --hash=sha256:fdf2e304f9e8864b8613591b18b36ee995560c9666033622eda1cb9057866880' \
        'botocore==1.43.106 --hash=sha256:c1fb8818f9957cb5037f73db34ac1a12ba43562e31d6e7f9cb7e5fc64e1dba78' \
        'catboost==1.2.10 --hash=sha256:42c1b6c7ae5c18cdbe00c8b9493987cc13338fe328baaf1a0b98ddaf58db96a2' \
        'certifi==2026.7.22 --hash=sha256:62f22742b58a1a33014a2b6b706588a8d7e2a88ae7bd1a6ebe8c992928483775' \
        'charset-normalizer==3.5.2 --hash=sha256:7218e8f32b0956cfcd048fd42d9d5779809745ca1d86113ca56f66e7ae1549c4' \
        'cloudpickle==3.1.2 --hash=sha256:9acb47f6afd73f60dc1df93bb801b472f05ff42fa6c84167d25cb206be1fbf4a' \
        'contourpy==1.4.0 --hash=sha256:f1219a8898523cba821085f2da8a1b962cc696325763f09d7f93538ba43b2d70' \
        'cycler==0.12.1 --hash=sha256:85cef7cff222d8644161529808465972e51340599459b8ac3ccbac5a854e0d30' \
        'et-xmlfile==2.0.0 --hash=sha256:7a91720bc756843502c3b7504c77b8fe44217c85c537d85037f0f536151b2caa' \
        'fonttools==4.66.1 --hash=sha256:83572afe48733bad7a4a9c11721d3a726c2e976d82b063fc9bdd049d76955abd' \
        'graphviz==0.21 --hash=sha256:54f33de9f4f911d7e84e4191749cac8cc5653f815b06738c54db9a15ab8b1e42' \
        'idna==3.20 --hash=sha256:ab7ae7122974553370f0bdb919e1a960b2cd1bc1ef0276416d896db81c14582c' \
        'jmespath==1.1.0 --hash=sha256:a5663118de4908c91729bea0acadca56526eb2698e83de10cd116ae0f4e97c64' \
        'joblib==1.6.0 --hash=sha256:3dbbf9f6e4b592a2357b854608e980fe6390d131d7a82f011a377ef2ebef7aba' \
        'kiwisolver==1.5.1 --hash=sha256:74ad5c3dad54a4641b4c28cd15ded70899d04459c6c7aeacafea716be97cce6d' \
        'lightgbm==4.6.0 --hash=sha256:cb19b5afea55b5b61cbb2131095f50538bd608a00655f23ad5d25ae3e3bf1c8d' \
        'matplotlib==3.10.9 --hash=sha256:8f3bcac1ca5ed000a6f4337d47ba67dfddf37ed6a46c15fd7f014997f7bf865f' \
        'narwhals==2.26.0 --hash=sha256:29326d74f107c347fd1009bd58e38d9f7c7c5b51e6de97bc93dbc325d9038b54' \
        'networkx==3.7 --hash=sha256:e3fd2c13a7814cee3746340d8d7f8598a67f16a58bf47fb7f8793fab6efca1b0' \
        'numpy==2.3.5 --hash=sha256:11e06aa0af8c0f05104d56450d6093ee639e15f24ecf62d417329d06e522e017' \
        'openpyxl==3.1.5 --hash=sha256:5282c12b107bffeef825f4617dc029afaf41d0ea60823bbb665ef3079dc79de2' \
        'packaging==26.3 --hash=sha256:d7193f7c8e4e93f444fde0262bf90af30e16fa0ad0ad44cb553c87339b23cd1c' \
        'pandas==2.3.3 --hash=sha256:318d77e0e42a628c04dc56bcef4b40de67918f7041c2b061af1da41dcff670ac' \
        'pillow==12.3.0 --hash=sha256:0847a763afefb695bc912d7c131e7e0632d4edc1d8698f58ddabec8e46b8b6d3' \
        'plotly==7.1.0 --hash=sha256:dbb7fa18afce40d0a8e80d1bf162eceb3faa0ce5a77fe741ad09a74cf78f53f3' \
        'psutil==7.1.3 --hash=sha256:3bb428f9f05c1225a558f53e30ccbad9930b11c3fc206836242de1091d3e7dd3' \
        'pyarrow==20.0.0 --hash=sha256:97c8dc984ed09cb07d618d57d8d4b67a5100a30c3818c2fb0b04599f0da2de7b' \
        'pyparsing==3.3.3 --hash=sha256:ece8c00a69cf01b45d0b1dedabb469c90d8caf996d4fda40f147627a122849a4' \
        'python-dateutil==2.9.0.post0 --hash=sha256:a8b2bc7bffae282281c8140a97d3aa9c14da0b136dfe83f850eea9a5f7470427' \
        'pytz==2026.4 --hash=sha256:9d514388fbc89ca0833203464272ac485b8828568ab73532f5020f17e892a0ff' \
        'PyYAML==6.0.3 --hash=sha256:0f29edc409a6392443abf94b9cf89ce99889a1dd5376d94316ae5145dfedd5d6' \
        'rdkit==2026.3.1 --hash=sha256:af2e141a7a885155ecf956adb04c26809146db8a8fc4ab1ad8946e108e174969' \
        'requests==2.34.2 --hash=sha256:2a0d60c172f83ac6ab31e4554906c0f3b3588d37b5cb939b1c061f4907e278e0' \
        's3transfer==0.19.2 --hash=sha256:d8168eccca828cbb2cd573675333f3bddd254313a9c42494b84c76b539e8ba25' \
        'scikit-learn==1.7.1 --hash=sha256:13679981fdaebc10cc4c13c43344416a86fcbc61449cb3e6517e1df9d12c8309' \
        'scipy==1.16.3 --hash=sha256:7dc1360c06535ea6116a2220f760ae572db9f661aba2d88074fe30ec2aa1ff88' \
        'six==1.17.0 --hash=sha256:4721f391ed90541fddacab5acf947aa0d3dc7d27b2e1e8eda2be8970586c3274' \
        'threadpoolctl==3.7.0 --hash=sha256:cd8b60b5641b45c67bbf73c64c843235fc2d8a480c87389f52f5dbee893b86be' \
        'tqdm==4.70.1 --hash=sha256:c293e525e6fef9c20e8728fd4612df02a0aa31bb5fe91ecd93e123b1b7bffa73' \
        'typing-extensions==4.16.0 --hash=sha256:481caa481374e813c1b176ada14e97f1f67a4539ce9cfeb3f350d78d6370c2e8' \
        'tzdata==2026.4 --hash=sha256:c2169a8b0a7a5e9674da5a135ccdfb2b3e671b333ed9fed17b41f73c34476e81' \
        'urllib3==2.8.0 --hash=sha256:0cf3cae568d36aa9576b28dfb35f11328f1cb974ca7647d9475ebb86c75ac6e3' \
        > "$WORK/py/requirements.lock"
    /usr/local/bin/python -m pip install --require-hashes --only-binary=:all: \
        --index-url https://pypi.org/simple \
        -r "$WORK/py/requirements.lock"
    /usr/local/bin/python -m pip check
    PYTHONPATH=/opt/mdcc /usr/local/bin/python -c 'from mdcc.core import check_runtime; check_runtime()'

    # Retain installed-version information with the image.
    /usr/local/bin/python -m pip freeze --all > /opt/mdcc/pip-freeze.txt
    dpkg-query -W > /opt/mdcc/os-packages.txt

    # Remove only the exact workspace created above; stop on any doubt.
    # Each check is a separate command so that set -e cannot skip a failure.
    [ "$WORK" = /__closha_build/work ] || fail "unexpected workspace path"
    [ ! -L "$BUILD_ROOT" ] || fail "parent is a symlink"
    [ ! -L "$WORK" ] || fail "workspace is a symlink"
    [ -d "$WORK" ] || fail "workspace is missing"
    [ "$(realpath -e -- "$WORK")" = "$WORK" ] || fail "canonical path changed"
    [ "$(stat -c %d -- "$WORK")" = "$(stat -c %d -- /)" ] || fail "workspace is on another filesystem"
    rm -rf --one-file-system -- "$WORK"
    rmdir -- "$BUILD_ROOT"

%runscript
    exec /usr/local/bin/python -m mdcc.cli train "$@"

%test
    set -eu
    export PATH=/usr/local/bin:/usr/bin:/bin
    export PYTHONPATH=/opt/mdcc
    export PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1
    export PYTHONNOUSERSITE=1
    export MPLBACKEND=Agg
    export LC_ALL=C.UTF-8

    # The build runs %test separately from %post, again with the host /tmp and
    # /var/tmp bound (mount tmp = yes), and R and Python create temporary
    # files there. When running as root (a root or fakeroot build), cover both,
    # and /dev/shm when present, with private tmpfs mounts first; if mounting
    # fails, the build stops.
    # Unprivileged runtime checks cannot mount and skip this step.
    if [ "$(id -u)" = 0 ]; then
        mount -t tmpfs -o mode=1777,nosuid,nodev closha-tmp /tmp
        mount -t tmpfs -o mode=1777,nosuid,nodev closha-vartmp /var/tmp
        [ "$(stat -f -c %T /tmp)" = tmpfs ] || { echo "/tmp is not private" >&2; exit 1; }
        [ "$(stat -f -c %T /var/tmp)" = tmpfs ] || { echo "/var/tmp is not private" >&2; exit 1; }
        if [ -d /dev/shm ]; then
            mount -t tmpfs -o mode=1777,nosuid,nodev closha-shm /dev/shm
            awk '$5 == "/dev/shm" { s = $0 } END { exit !(s ~ / - tmpfs closha-shm /) }' /proc/self/mountinfo ||
                { echo "/dev/shm is not private" >&2; exit 1; }
        fi
    fi

    [ "$(command -v python)" = /usr/local/bin/python ]
    python -c 'from mdcc.core import check_runtime; check_runtime()'
    python -c 'import rdkit, autogluon.tabular, lightgbm, catboost, sklearn, scipy, matplotlib, openpyxl'
    python -m mdcc.cli train --help >/dev/null

    # The build workspace must not remain in the image.
    if [ -e /__closha_build ]; then
        echo 'Build workspace /__closha_build remains in the image' >&2
        exit 1
    fi

    echo 'RTpred train: runtime dependency checks passed.'

%help
    RTpred (Retip) train module: Python 3.13.15 (Debian 12 slim), hash-locked
    PyPI wheels (rdkit, autogluon.tabular, LightGBM, CatBoost, scikit-learn),
    and the embedded mdcc package.

    The CLOSHA build system builds this DEF with its fixed Slurm job (policy
    section 6.2) from its --chdir directory, where mdcc/ (without __pycache__)
    must be uploaded first, since %files paths are relative to it:
        apptainer build bx_retip_train.1.0.sif bx_retip_train.1.0.def
    It must pass both as root and with fakeroot.
    Build from a shell without APPTAINER_* or SINGULARITY_* bind variables.

    Check and run the image:
        apptainer test --cleanenv bx_retip_train.1.0.sif
        apptainer run bx_retip_train.1.0.sif --help
    Output directories must be empty. Runtime analysis needs no network.
